# Trivy ignore list for the runtime image scan in .github/workflows/ci.yml.
#
# The scan fails CI on HIGH/CRITICAL findings that have a fix available
# (`ignore-unfixed: true`), so anything listed here is a deliberate, reviewed
# decision to ship a known-vulnerable component — not a way to quiet the build.
#
# Every entry MUST carry, on the lines above it:
#   * why the finding does not apply to this deployment (or why the fix cannot
#     be taken yet), and
#   * an expiry date, after which the entry is removed and the finding is
#     either fixed or re-justified.
#
# Format is one CVE id per line, optionally with an expiry:
#   CVE-2024-12345 exp:2026-12-31
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# npm's own bundled dependencies, shipped inside node:24-bookworm-slim at
# /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/. NOT application dependencies:
# the scan reports 0 vulnerabilities for every path under /app and 0 for the
# Debian package set — these five are entirely the base image's npm CLI.
#
# Why they do not apply here: all five are denial-of-service vectors that
# require feeding hostile input to npm (a crafted gzip/tar archive, a crafted
# brace pattern, an attacker-controlled HTTP response). Nothing in the running
# container executes npm at all — the CMD invokes the Prisma CLI through node
# directly and the app never shells out to a package manager. Reaching these
# code paths would require an attacker who can already run commands in the
# container, at which point the CVE is irrelevant.
#
# Why the fix cannot be taken yet: "fixed" here means the upstream library has
# a patched release, not that npm has shipped a build bundling it. Upgrading
# npm inside the image would only trade these for whatever the next npm
# bundles. The real fix is a newer node base image; re-check at expiry.
#
# exp: 2026-10-31 — re-verify against the then-current node:24-bookworm-slim
# and delete any entry the base image has resolved.
CVE-2026-59873 exp:2026-10-31
CVE-2026-59874 exp:2026-10-31
CVE-2026-13149 exp:2026-10-31
CVE-2026-14257 exp:2026-10-31
CVE-2026-12151 exp:2026-10-31
